  "freshBundledObservations": [
    {
      "caseId": "c02-collateral-interest",
      "requestedModel": "openai/gpt-5.2",
      "question": "Compare how supplying a supported non-base collateral asset can earn protocol supply interest in the Aave V3 Ethereum Pool versus the Compound III Ethereum USDC Comet. Exclude token staking yield and incentive rewards from this question.",
      "startedAt": "2026-11-12T17:35:12.164Z",
      "finishedAt": "2026-11-12T17:35:23.292Z",
      "journal": {
        "file": "plugin-foundations-review3-c02-collateral-interest.jsonl",
        "sha256": "9426e8d073cd07fd007d281c8bdc9ed13c63efbfdf60632fd5884a48325e4796"
      },
      "resultSha256": "4b1ab65c38fb6b42fe55514aa9997d660b04137e0758f901a4a78c61707a15a7",
      "result": {
        "status": "answered",
        "answer": "Aave V3 Ethereum Pool:\nIn the Aave V3 Ethereum Pool, supplying a supported reserve asset (including a non-base collateral asset) mints the corresponding aTokens to the supplier, and the aToken balance is designed to represent a supply position with interest accrual via the reserve’s liquidity index. The reserve’s normalized supply income is updated over time using the current liquidity rate, and that liquidity rate is derived from borrower activity (it is based on the borrowing rate, scaled by utilization and adjusted by the reserve factor; with no debt, the liquidity rate calculation returns zero). As a result, a supplied non-base collateral asset can earn protocol supply interest (excluding incentives) through this reserve-index/aToken mechanism, but the interest depends on utilization/borrowing rather than being fixed or guaranteed.\n\nCompound III Ethereum USDC Comet:\nIn the Compound III Ethereum USDC Comet, supplying an accepted non-base collateral asset increases borrowing capacity (subject to its collateral factor and supply cap), but the collateral asset itself does not earn protocol interest merely for being supplied. Protocol interest (excluding incentives) is associated with the market’s base asset: a positive base-asset balance earns interest under the base-asset supply rate model, while a negative base balance accrues borrowing interest; rates depend on utilization. Therefore, supplying supported non-base collateral in this USDC market does not earn protocol supply interest, whereas supplying (and holding a positive balance of) the base asset does.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "id": "aave-v3-ethereum-identity",
            "url": "https://github.com/aave-dao/aave-address-book/blob/b8c801a413c4b934afaf7976d2ddc5fbada6dce6/src/ts/AaveV3Ethereum.ts",
